<%# The action summary of the "Indexierung" page (doc/ki_bereich_navigation_plan.md §3.5).

    What this replaces: a page that opened with eight raw counters and left the admin to
    work out from them whether anything was broken. The table below is unchanged and
    still the detail; this says in words what the numbers add up to, and carries the one
    action that helps.

    Three things it must get right, all three learned rather than invented:

    * The figures come from Embeddings::IndexHealth, the SAME source as the hub card, so
      the two surfaces can never disagree about a backlog. Not from @sync_statistics,
      which counts per project and would be a second derivation of the same rule.
    * The state is asked through IndexHealth::Result#clear? / #working? — the predicates
      that already carry the rule. Re-deriving :ok/:working/:alert from pending/failed
      here would put it in a third place, and the copy in a view is the one nobody tests.
    * A running staged switch is stated SEPARATELY rather than instead of the backlog
      (§3.5 Fortschreibung). It explains why numbers move; it does not excuse failures,
      and hiding a failure behind "ein Wechsel läuft" is exactly how this page would go
      back to being unreadable.

    ⚠️ #working? is a claim about the BACKLOG, never about the queue serving it. It reads
    a positive pending count with no failures as progress, which is only true while a job
    worker exists — and IndexHealth cannot know that (it counts content columns, and the
    queue tables carry no organisation, so it must not learn to). A dead queue therefore
    rendered as "wird verarbeitet" for as long as it stayed dead. Embeddings::IndexingPipeline
    is the missing second input: it DEMOTES a working state to :alert and says why. That is
    a new input, not the forbidden re-derivation above — the pending/failed rules still live
    in exactly one place, this only refuses to call an unattended backlog progress.

    Locals: none — reads @index_health, @switch_progress, @indexing_pipeline,
    @current_organisation. %>
<%# paused FIRST: over an AI-off organisation neither "alles verarbeitet" nor
    "Verarbeitung läuft" is true, and no button on this page changes it. A stall is not
    news there either — nobody is supposed to be working. %>
<% paused = @index_health.paused? %>
<% stalled = !paused && @index_health.pending.positive? && @indexing_pipeline.stalled? %>
<% state = if paused then :paused
           elsif @index_health.clear? then :ok
           elsif @index_health.working? && !stalled then :working
           else :alert
           end %>
<% tone = { ok: 'bg-green-500', working: 'bg-cobalt-500', alert: 'bg-red-500', paused: 'bg-cream-400' }[state] %>
<%# A stall reaches :alert with nothing failed, and "Es sind Fehler aufgetreten" would then
    name a defect the counts do not show. Its own heading, so the red dot keeps meaning
    "act on this" without the sentence claiming the wrong reason. %>
<% heading_key = { ok: 'clear', working: 'pending', alert: 'failed', paused: 'paused' }[state] %>
<% heading_key = 'stalled' if state == :alert && @index_health.failed.zero? && stalled %>
<% heading = t("views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.heading_#{heading_key}") %>
<% switch_running = @switch_progress.present? && @switch_progress.in_progress? %>

<div class="rounded-lg border-2 border-ink bg-white p-5 shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#000000]"
     data-index-summary-state="<%= state %>">
  <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
    <span class="mt-1.5 h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rounded-full <%= tone %>" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold leading-tight text-cream-900"><%= heading %></h2>

      <div class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm text-cream-700">
        <%# The counts stay VISIBLE while paused — they are true, they are just not a
            backlog anybody owes. Hiding them would trade one wrong impression for
            another, namely that there is nothing here at all. %>
        <% if paused %>
          <p><%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.body_paused') %></p>
        <% end %>
        <% if @index_health.clear? && !paused %>
          <p><%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.body_clear') %></p>
        <% end %>
        <% if @index_health.failed.positive? %>
          <p class="font-medium text-red-700">
            <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.failed', count: @index_health.failed) %>
          </p>
        <% end %>
        <% if @index_health.pending.positive? %>
          <p><%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.pending', count: @index_health.pending) %></p>
        <% end %>
        <%# The sentence that stops "vorgemerkt" from reading as "under way". Placed right
            after the pending count it qualifies, because apart it is just another warning
            and the admin would still press the button that enqueues into a dead queue. %>
        <% if stalled %>
          <p class="font-medium text-red-700">
            <i class="bi bi-pause-circle mr-1"></i>
            <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.stalled') %>
          </p>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <%# Which space the counts describe. nil covers "no credential" as well as a
          broken pin — both are operator findings (embeddings:check_alignment), and both
          are worth saying out loud here rather than leaving the numbers unqualified. %>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-cream-500">
        <% if @index_health.space %>
          <i class="bi bi-diagram-3 mr-1"></i>
          <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.space',
                provider: @index_health.space[:embedding_provider],
                model: @index_health.space[:embedding_model],
                dims: @index_health.space[:embedding_dims]) %>
        <% else %>
          <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle mr-1"></i>
          <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.space_unknown') %>
        <% end %>
      </p>

      <% if switch_running %>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-md border border-cobalt-300 bg-cobalt-50 p-3"
             data-switch-state="<%= @switch_progress.state %>">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-cobalt-900">
            <i class="bi bi-arrow-left-right mr-1.5"></i>
            <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.switch.heading') %>
          </p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-cobalt-900">
            <%= t("views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.switch.#{@switch_progress.state}",
                  completed: number_with_delimiter(@switch_progress.completed),
                  total: number_with_delimiter(@switch_progress.total),
                  percent: @switch_progress.percent) %>
          </p>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# The action, next to the sentence that motivates it — that pairing is the whole
          point of the summary. "Neu verarbeiten" is a catch-up run, so it is offered
          whenever something is outstanding or failed, and replaced by a plain statement
          when there is genuinely nothing to press.

          Off-palette handmade buttons are what the P4/AP5 pass removed from this page;
          both keep going through ButtonComponent. Reprocess stays the consequential
          action (primary, confirm: it enqueues a mass job), refresh the neutral one. %>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <%# No catch-up run while paused: it would extract for the full-text index and
            embed nothing, so the button would keep offering itself forever. The way out
            of this state is the switch, not this page. %>
        <% unless @index_health.clear? || paused %>
          <%= render Neo::Buttons::ButtonComponent.new(
                variant: :primary,
                size: :medium,
                icon: 'play-fill',
                confirm: t('views.confirm.reprocess_embeddings'),
                form: {
                  action: reprocess_embeddings_organisation_ai_sync_status_path(@current_organisation),
                  method: :post
                }
              ) do %>
            <%= t('views.organisations.ai_sync_statuses.show.reprocess_embeddings') %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>

        <%= render Neo::Buttons::ButtonComponent.new(
              variant: :secondary,
              size: :medium,
              icon: 'arrow-clockwise',
              url: organisation_ai_sync_status_path(@current_organisation)
            ) do %>
          <%= t('views.organisations.ai_sync_statuses.show.refresh_status') %>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-cream-500">
        <%= if paused
              t('views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.paused_hint')
            elsif @index_health.clear?
              t('views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.nothing_to_do')
            else
              t('views.organisations.ai_overview.index_summary.action_hint')
            end %>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
